WEBVTT

00:03.050 --> 00:05.770
Oh, my God, it's so cute.

00:06.170 --> 00:08.390
I have to wave this around?

00:08.390 --> 00:09.840
Kanae, want to use this?

00:09.840 --> 00:10.920
I'm using this.

00:10.920 --> 00:13.110
I'm not really...

00:13.110 --> 00:14.730
Don't worry.

00:14.730 --> 00:18.160
I told you, the performance and the
girls' day out today is all on me.

00:18.750 --> 00:20.720
And this and this.

00:20.720 --> 00:22.120
I don't want to impose.

00:23.020 --> 00:24.710
It's going to be the agency paying.

00:25.130 --> 00:28.480
I don't like throwing out gifts,
even after the break-up.

00:28.480 --> 00:29.340
What about you?

00:29.340 --> 00:31.150
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:31.150 --> 00:35.130
Please, I'm trying to have a heart-to-heart
with you right now, dear.

00:35.130 --> 00:37.040
That's the whole point of a girls' day out.

00:37.040 --> 00:39.930
Again, I've never been on
a girls' day out before.

00:39.930 --> 00:42.200
Besides, Liszt-san, you used to be a guy.

00:43.610 --> 00:46.820
Want to buy a swimsuit, my little kitten?

00:47.730 --> 00:50.230
How do you expect me to wear that thing?

00:51.030 --> 00:52.920
That's from your school club, isn't it?

00:52.920 --> 00:54.600
I-It's comfortable to swim in.

00:54.900 --> 00:57.490
I'll say it again: It's all

00:57.490 --> 00:59.140
on me today.

00:59.140 --> 01:00.830
I'm fine with this one.

01:00.830 --> 01:02.300
Huh?

01:02.770 --> 01:04.750
I didn't know they were here.

01:05.210 --> 01:08.840
All on Liszt-san? That's no fair.

01:08.840 --> 01:12.400
The Claskey Klasky concert
will be beginning shortly.

01:12.700 --> 01:14.010
Oh, yeah!

01:14.940 --> 01:16.470
A concert at a pool?

01:16.470 --> 01:20.110
When can we stop doing these
weak-sauce local gigs?

01:20.110 --> 01:22.380
We're busy enough with

01:22.380 --> 01:24.270
our recordings and our national tour.

01:25.080 --> 01:26.600
That hurts, damn it!

01:26.890 --> 01:28.980
Would you like some gyoza?

01:28.980 --> 01:30.540
Woo! Tchaggo-chan!

01:30.540 --> 01:31.480
Bądako!

01:32.040 --> 01:33.910
They don't even get our names right.

01:35.480 --> 01:38.340
I wish that man would find us better gigs.

01:38.340 --> 01:39.990
You know?

01:40.290 --> 01:43.900
I don't know if people really
appreciate our work.

01:44.430 --> 01:45.620
Nah.

01:47.050 --> 01:47.940
Let's go.

01:48.560 --> 01:50.950
Wait, Tchaiko-chan.

02:08.830 --> 02:11.900
They're actually pretty awesome.

02:17.640 --> 02:20.830
Epic! Godly performance!

02:20.830 --> 02:23.490
Bąda! Tchaiko!

02:24.210 --> 02:27.500
So <i>this</i> is a girls' day out.

02:28.070 --> 02:30.410
You've made my dream come true, Kanae.

02:30.410 --> 02:31.470
Thanks.

02:31.470 --> 02:32.720
Nah.

02:32.720 --> 02:34.510
I got to swim and watch a good show.

02:34.510 --> 02:36.210
It was so fun.

02:36.710 --> 02:39.240
But does this really count
as a girls' day out?

02:39.650 --> 02:41.940
How am I supposed to talk to them

02:41.940 --> 02:43.970
if they keep calling it a girls' day out?

02:43.970 --> 02:45.690
Okay, I think we should head...

02:45.010 --> 02:46.320
Oh, there they are.

02:47.010 --> 02:48.610
Over here.

02:51.190 --> 02:53.730
Long time, Tchaiko, Bąda.

02:52.930 --> 02:53.730
No!

02:54.120 --> 02:55.190
Tchaiko?

02:55.190 --> 02:55.980
Bąda?

02:55.980 --> 02:59.070
Shh! Keep it down!

02:59.070 --> 03:00.800
What if there's a fan?

03:00.800 --> 03:03.450
Stop... I can't breathe.

03:04.210 --> 03:05.200
For real?!

03:05.740 --> 03:08.950
Now, let's get this girls' day out started.

03:10.140 --> 03:11.380
We're starting now?

04:44.380 --> 04:49.140
08: "Girls' Day Out"

04:46.060 --> 04:49.510
"Come hang with us for a girls' day out"...

04:49.990 --> 04:53.110
What am I supposed to do
with a message like that?

04:53.110 --> 04:54.440
I know.

04:54.440 --> 04:57.200
We're pretty busy, you know.

04:57.200 --> 04:59.650
I don't know anyone else
I could invite, though.

05:00.510 --> 05:03.130
It was your choice to leave the agency.
You're talking crazy.

05:03.730 --> 05:06.180
You've got some serious nerve.

05:06.180 --> 05:07.910
Why did you come, then?

05:07.910 --> 05:10.010
I thought you had something
important to say.

05:08.500 --> 05:10.520
We have more girls here,

05:10.420 --> 05:13.410
Come on, we're having fun.

05:10.520 --> 05:13.130
but this isn't a very good
vibe for a girls' day out.

05:16.040 --> 05:17.470
So do you have a boyfriend?

05:17.470 --> 05:18.990
Why would I?

05:18.990 --> 05:20.840
Don't you at least have a crush on someone?

05:20.840 --> 05:22.630
I don't have the time.

05:23.140 --> 05:24.920
Are you sure you aren't overworked?

05:24.920 --> 05:26.820
I don't hate my job.

05:29.300 --> 05:31.400
You girls are so boring.

05:31.400 --> 05:32.910
This is supposed to be a girls' day out.

05:32.910 --> 05:34.410
Not to mention, I'm paying.

05:34.410 --> 05:35.360
Do you get it?

05:35.990 --> 05:38.320
It's the agency paying anyway.

05:38.320 --> 05:39.860
That's such a loveless thing to say.

05:49.480 --> 05:52.940
Okay, fine, Kanae, <i>you </i>
say something intense.

05:52.940 --> 05:54.640
We see each other every day.

05:54.640 --> 05:56.490
I don't know what to say.

05:56.490 --> 05:59.020
Give me a dark, complicated doozy
from the depths of your mind.

05:59.020 --> 06:01.170
I've got nothing. I'm not that grim.

06:03.730 --> 06:07.300
So anyway, Cho-chan's
girlfriend at the time...

06:07.560 --> 06:10.150
She had a seriously crazy love life.

06:10.150 --> 06:11.470
She was pretty weird.

06:12.030 --> 06:16.230
I mean, I dated her a
little bit, too, actually.

06:16.780 --> 06:20.480
It's been over a century, though.
I think she gets a pass.

06:20.480 --> 06:21.620
Uh...

06:21.620 --> 06:24.120
This is the sixth time
you've told me this story.

06:24.120 --> 06:25.920
No way! It's only the third time.

06:25.920 --> 06:27.820
Once is enough.

06:32.080 --> 06:33.190
Fine.

06:33.190 --> 06:34.280
I'll buy you something in return.

06:34.580 --> 06:35.400
Huh?

06:38.330 --> 06:40.830
No, it's okay, I swear.

06:41.080 --> 06:43.260
It doesn't cost anything to
just try it on. Come on.

06:43.260 --> 06:44.040
Eh?

06:44.860 --> 06:48.420
I was kind enough to invite you to my
girls' day out with my little kitten.

06:49.150 --> 06:51.610
So why the attitude?

06:51.610 --> 06:54.890
I should have just made it a
date for the two of us.

06:54.890 --> 06:58.890
Give me a break. I didn't think
that girl would be here.

06:58.890 --> 07:00.020
Exactly.

07:00.020 --> 07:01.480
I was shocked when I got here.

07:01.850 --> 07:03.910
Are you telling me it's my
little kitten's fault?

07:04.450 --> 07:06.230
I'm changed.

07:07.320 --> 07:08.810
How do I look?

07:11.280 --> 07:11.820
Next.

07:12.080 --> 07:12.940
What?!

07:13.600 --> 07:16.300
She doesn't know, though, does she?

07:16.300 --> 07:16.700
Know what?

07:17.180 --> 07:19.920
That we were the ones
who attacked the mansion

07:19.920 --> 07:21.470
and sent the mice after her.

07:21.470 --> 07:22.710
Well, yeah.

07:23.090 --> 07:24.810
We're technically enemies.

07:24.810 --> 07:27.630
How are we supposed to be
all smiley and friendly?

07:29.140 --> 07:31.680
This one's a little too much for me.

07:34.870 --> 07:35.470
Next.

07:35.670 --> 07:36.860
Shock!

07:39.080 --> 07:41.000
To be honest,

07:41.000 --> 07:44.110
you guys didn't actually want
to mess with her, did you?

07:44.110 --> 07:45.270
I can see right through you.

07:47.680 --> 07:48.860
That's not true.

07:49.180 --> 07:52.610
Just admit it already.

07:52.830 --> 07:56.620
I already know you have a lot to say.

07:56.860 --> 07:58.870
You repressed wench!

07:59.420 --> 08:00.750
Did you know?!

08:00.750 --> 08:03.540
That I'm frustrate—

08:05.170 --> 08:05.830
Huh?

08:08.670 --> 08:09.280
Huh?

08:09.830 --> 08:11.260
Let's buy that.

08:11.260 --> 08:13.090
Karaoke Room

08:15.090 --> 08:18.840
Monday, we spend at a fan meet

08:18.840 --> 08:22.630
And we get scolded for being rude

08:22.630 --> 08:26.350
Tuesday, we forget our lyrics

08:26.350 --> 08:30.100
We hummed the melody, but it was no use

08:30.100 --> 08:33.840
Wednesday, we stayed up all
night signing autographs

08:33.840 --> 08:37.590
Smeared with the blood
from our chapped hands

08:37.590 --> 08:41.360
Thursday, we arrive late at the venue

08:41.360 --> 08:45.130
We get yelled at for being slow and stupid

08:45.130 --> 08:48.850
Friday, we have dance lessons

08:48.850 --> 08:52.600
My heels are so high, I sprained my ankle

08:52.600 --> 08:56.340
Saturday, the pain still won't go away

08:56.340 --> 09:00.060
I chipped a tooth clenching really hard

09:00.060 --> 09:03.810
Sunday, I figured I should
call my parents back home

09:03.810 --> 09:07.560
Oh, wait, I don't have a home to call

09:07.560 --> 09:11.320
This is a week in my life

09:11.320 --> 09:15.070
Oh the pain, the pain, the pain!

09:21.880 --> 09:23.160
I knew it.

09:23.780 --> 09:25.800
You two <i>do</i> hate work.

09:25.800 --> 09:27.750
It's a Russian folk song.

09:28.050 --> 09:30.060
Those couldn't have been the original lyrics.

09:30.060 --> 09:30.750
I get it!

09:30.980 --> 09:31.920
What?

09:32.200 --> 09:35.180
Your song is so touching,

09:35.800 --> 09:38.090
Tchaiko-san, Bąda-san.

09:39.490 --> 09:41.290
Our song?

09:41.590 --> 09:43.560
Was touching?

09:45.350 --> 09:46.790
It was.

09:46.790 --> 09:48.620
No matter how hard you try...

09:48.940 --> 09:52.820
Men will just never understand!

09:52.820 --> 09:56.540
Monday, I spend all day cleaning up

09:56.540 --> 10:00.320
Tuesday, Motes-san makes a mess

10:00.320 --> 10:04.070
Wednesday, Beethes starts a fire

10:04.070 --> 10:07.790
Thursday, the contractors
come to wreck the place

10:07.790 --> 10:11.490
Weekend, I get paid the rent,

10:11.490 --> 10:15.170
but the only one paying is Liszt-san

10:15.170 --> 10:19.090
Oh the pain, the pain, the pain, the pain!

10:19.090 --> 10:22.600
The pain, the pain, the pain!

10:22.850 --> 10:26.520
The pain, the pain, the pain!

10:26.520 --> 10:29.960
The pain, the pain, the pain!

10:29.960 --> 10:31.010
One more time!

10:30.300 --> 10:34.080
The pain, the pain, the pain!

10:32.610 --> 10:37.420
Damn it, get all the men out of the house!

10:34.080 --> 10:37.860
The pain, the pain, the pain!

10:34.690 --> 10:37.420
Yes, my little kitten...

10:37.860 --> 10:39.570
Yes!

10:40.420 --> 10:43.120
Hasshie, are you a girl? A boy?

10:43.800 --> 10:46.120
Not that I care at all,

10:46.590 --> 10:48.810
but you can't tell from looking
at its ass, you know.

10:49.540 --> 10:51.920
Keep Closed!!

10:55.130 --> 10:56.460
Senpai...

10:56.920 --> 10:58.680
When will you come out of hiding?

10:59.430 --> 11:01.430
Karaoke Room

10:59.430 --> 11:02.220
The pain, the pain, the pain!

11:02.220 --> 11:05.970
The pain, the pain, the pain!

11:02.840 --> 11:05.700
Yes! More confessions!

11:05.700 --> 11:07.390
Seriously!

11:05.970 --> 11:09.810
The pain, the pain, the pain!

11:07.390 --> 11:10.280
You can't be serious with that freaking wig!

11:13.870 --> 11:15.350
I said it.

11:15.350 --> 11:18.500
I can't go back anymore.

11:18.500 --> 11:19.620
It's all right.

11:20.250 --> 11:21.580
You did the right thing.

11:21.580 --> 11:22.700
Exactly!

11:22.930 --> 11:24.370
It's a girls' day out!

11:24.370 --> 11:28.040
Let's make confessions and lose our shit!

11:31.040 --> 11:33.360
Yay!

11:33.360 --> 11:35.020
This is it!

11:35.020 --> 11:37.300
This is a real girls' day out!

11:35.980 --> 11:39.680
The pain, the pain, the pain!

11:37.300 --> 11:38.210
I think.

11:39.680 --> 11:43.210
The pain, the pain, the pain!

11:40.400 --> 11:43.750
Wh-What's the deal with girls' days out?

11:54.400 --> 11:55.500
Really?

11:55.500 --> 11:58.750
You two have dirt on

11:58.750 --> 12:00.280
Beethes and Motes?

12:00.520 --> 12:01.910
Do I?

12:01.910 --> 12:03.160
Those guys are, like...

12:08.000 --> 12:10.250
Oh yeah, one time, Chopin
was all by himself...

12:14.330 --> 12:16.340
Not to mention, Schu...

12:23.280 --> 12:25.870
I can't really hear them,

12:25.870 --> 12:28.850
but it sounds like they're
rejecting everyone's humanity.

12:29.180 --> 12:32.100
I mean, none of them are
even human to begin with.

12:32.330 --> 12:34.810
Well, Sousuke's technically human.

12:34.810 --> 12:36.020
Technically?!

12:36.020 --> 12:38.080
That's the thing though, what a shame.

12:38.080 --> 12:39.280
I know, right?

12:39.280 --> 12:40.630
What a loser.

12:40.630 --> 12:42.070
Lame.

12:42.310 --> 12:44.180
He's a tool, after all.

12:44.600 --> 12:46.440
What do you want me to do?!

12:50.440 --> 12:53.120
Cheers!

12:55.050 --> 12:56.080
Yum.

12:56.080 --> 12:58.240
Are you sure about renting out

12:58.240 --> 13:00.730
a boat on the agency's credit card?

13:00.730 --> 13:02.660
It's their fault for not freezing it.

13:02.960 --> 13:04.840
Gotta make use of it while I can.

13:05.350 --> 13:09.510
That man won't even notice these expenses.

13:09.900 --> 13:12.270
This wouldn't even
put a dent in what he's got.

13:12.270 --> 13:14.960
I-Is he <i>that</i> wealthy?

13:15.260 --> 13:16.770
Yeah, I guess.

13:17.290 --> 13:21.690
Money means little to as great a man as him.

13:21.690 --> 13:24.570
You must really admire him.

13:26.190 --> 13:28.910
Say, if you like him so much,

13:29.480 --> 13:31.080
why don't you date him?

13:31.340 --> 13:32.070
Huh?

13:34.680 --> 13:37.260
No way, no way. He's an old fart.

13:41.680 --> 13:43.220
Gah...

13:43.220 --> 13:44.740
Yo, Boss, get me some shiokara!

13:45.040 --> 13:47.630
Tch-Tchaiko-chan, you're
regressing into geezer mode.

13:47.630 --> 13:48.180
Eh?

13:48.420 --> 13:50.000
Geezer mode?

13:50.310 --> 13:53.760
She always does this when
she thinks about that man.

13:54.820 --> 13:56.350
Shiokara?

13:56.350 --> 13:57.350
This is a French restaurant.

13:59.060 --> 14:02.160
And you, Liszt-chan, why
are you drinking wine?

14:02.460 --> 14:04.770
I'm an adult in this story.

14:06.300 --> 14:07.850
That's BS!

14:07.850 --> 14:11.820
Why is it that, just because they wrote me
as a teen, I have to have ginger ale?!

14:11.820 --> 14:13.410
Why do you get all the good stuff?!

14:13.410 --> 14:15.160
What the hell's the problem?!

14:14.000 --> 14:15.450
Tchaiko-chan, stop.

14:15.450 --> 14:16.770
What if someone sees you?

14:16.770 --> 14:18.170
Shut up, you one-hit wonder!

14:19.130 --> 14:20.970
One-hit wonder...

14:23.270 --> 14:24.860
I'm quitting!

14:24.860 --> 14:26.340
Calm down!

14:26.600 --> 14:28.980
How am I supposed to stay calm?!

14:28.400 --> 14:30.480
That's my line!

14:30.700 --> 14:31.780
Oh, yeah?!

14:31.300 --> 14:32.210
What are...

14:32.210 --> 14:34.190
Oh, God, what's happening?

14:34.190 --> 14:35.740
Sousuke, Sousuke.

14:37.240 --> 14:41.740
Here's a search result for "Bąda
one-hit wonder composer."

14:42.920 --> 14:46.110
Tekla Bądarzewska?

14:46.430 --> 14:48.910
She's a Polish composer who became

14:48.910 --> 14:52.660
famous worldwide for just one
piece: "A Maiden's Prayer."

14:53.060 --> 14:54.870
I've heard this piece before.

14:55.390 --> 14:58.330
So Bąda-chan's a ClassicaLoid, too?

14:58.330 --> 15:00.460
Also, I tried searching for Tchaiko,

15:00.460 --> 15:03.800
excluding results regarding Claskey Klasky.

15:04.560 --> 15:06.280
Check it out.

15:07.380 --> 15:12.590
Pyotr Tchaikovsky

15:07.590 --> 15:09.510
Pyotr Tchaikovsky.

15:09.510 --> 15:12.590
A great Russian composer from the 1800s.

15:13.280 --> 15:16.350
Tchaiko is this beardo?!

15:17.320 --> 15:19.150
Quit lying to me!

15:19.150 --> 15:21.270
I don't tell lies!

15:19.430 --> 15:20.950
Yo, Boss, over here!

15:21.540 --> 15:23.200
Vodka. <i>Ice</i> cold.

15:23.200 --> 15:25.020
No! You're underage!

15:25.560 --> 15:26.970
Cancel that order.

15:26.970 --> 15:27.680
Yes, ma'am.

15:27.680 --> 15:30.000
I'm not playing a cute girl by choice.

15:30.000 --> 15:31.740
I need to drink, or I'll go insane.

15:32.080 --> 15:34.460
Remember when I said, "If you
drink, we're breaking up"?

15:34.460 --> 15:35.580
Remember that?

15:35.950 --> 15:38.160
Fine by me. Let's break up.

15:38.160 --> 15:39.500
I want to go back.

15:39.500 --> 15:42.220
I want to go back to being
a normal bearded dude.

15:42.220 --> 15:43.130
Hey!

15:43.130 --> 15:45.190
Please don't say that!

15:43.610 --> 15:45.880
You're kidding me.

15:44.260 --> 15:45.880
Shut up, we're breaking up!

15:46.260 --> 15:47.610
Oh, dear.

15:47.610 --> 15:50.370
Do girls' days out always end up like this?

15:50.370 --> 15:51.970
I don't think so.

15:51.970 --> 15:54.420
I think this has turned into something else.

15:58.100 --> 16:01.100
Incoming Call

15:58.760 --> 16:00.390
It's from that man.

16:03.220 --> 16:04.530
What do we do?

16:08.860 --> 16:10.740
I'm answering it on speakerphone.

16:11.970 --> 16:14.700
This is the highlight of
the girls' day out today.

16:16.080 --> 16:19.370
Tell him exactly what you want to tell him.

16:19.810 --> 16:21.090
I support you.

16:21.090 --> 16:22.000
Tchaiko-chan.

16:24.750 --> 16:27.250
Connected

16:30.050 --> 16:32.040
H-Hullo?

16:32.330 --> 16:33.510
Lentezza!

16:37.870 --> 16:41.960
I-I'm sorry.

16:42.770 --> 16:45.020
Connected

16:43.050 --> 16:44.670
Stretto.

16:45.510 --> 16:48.330
I'm truly sorry.

16:48.330 --> 16:49.590
Stretto.

16:49.590 --> 16:51.310
Forgive me.

16:51.310 --> 16:54.030
I meant to come home right away.

16:55.850 --> 16:58.220
She's totally under his control.

16:58.790 --> 17:02.750
Wh-Who is that guy calling her?

17:03.600 --> 17:05.000
Oh, I see.

17:05.260 --> 17:06.460
He's the Claskey Klasky...

17:07.670 --> 17:09.170
Cut it out!

17:09.170 --> 17:11.640
You're the freak of a manager that

17:11.640 --> 17:14.430
messed up my Tchaiko and Bąda-kyun!

17:14.740 --> 17:15.880
Sousuke?

17:17.110 --> 17:18.760
Riposatamente.

17:18.760 --> 17:21.430
I have no idea what the hell you're saying.

17:21.430 --> 17:22.990
Talk normally!

17:22.990 --> 17:24.490
They're both crying.

17:24.490 --> 17:27.740
They're developing a creepy
old man split personality!

17:27.740 --> 17:30.360
What good is an agency, if you can't
even take care of your artists?

17:30.760 --> 17:32.280
Say something, asshole!

17:32.610 --> 17:34.280
Who the hell do you think you are?

17:36.460 --> 17:37.900
Bach-sama.

17:38.930 --> 17:40.800
It's the producer of Claskey Klasky,

17:40.800 --> 17:43.650
Johann Sebastian Bach,
that you're talking to.

17:43.650 --> 17:44.420
Wha?

17:45.440 --> 17:46.950
Bach?!

17:46.950 --> 17:48.600
The genius?

17:48.600 --> 17:52.340
That super-famous, currently
trending man that I admire?

17:52.340 --> 17:55.670
He wasn't just a manager or something?

18:04.060 --> 18:08.310
Connected

18:04.650 --> 18:07.990
I respect your talent.

18:08.870 --> 18:11.700
But as an

18:12.240 --> 18:15.320
artist myself...

18:16.060 --> 18:17.030
Amazing.

18:17.900 --> 18:19.570
Keep going, tool.

18:20.070 --> 18:21.830
I have something to tell you!

18:24.880 --> 18:26.220
Sousuke...

18:25.850 --> 18:28.360
I...

18:26.560 --> 18:28.060
What's gotten into you?

18:28.360 --> 18:30.500
t-t-t-truly...

18:30.910 --> 18:32.430
I believe...

18:34.180 --> 18:37.850
It must be love!

18:54.380 --> 18:57.360
The courage to confess is love itself.

18:57.750 --> 19:01.160
With that power, we could all go further.

19:04.220 --> 19:05.580
To be honest,

19:05.940 --> 19:08.840
you've got to be a really crappy producer

19:08.840 --> 19:11.830
to scare away your artists.

19:12.360 --> 19:13.920
Give it to him!

19:14.220 --> 19:16.420
Even more!

19:16.860 --> 19:18.880
The girl's night out is love.

19:18.880 --> 19:21.270
A stage for the thoughts that

19:19.250 --> 19:23.180
Yahoo!

19:21.270 --> 19:23.180
we can otherwise never express.

19:24.550 --> 19:26.890
We're all dispensable, aren't we?

19:27.210 --> 19:29.350
You monster!

19:30.370 --> 19:31.810
Go, Tchai!

19:32.350 --> 19:36.340
You don't even have any hopes
for my music or lyrics, do you?

19:34.060 --> 19:37.820
Connected

19:36.340 --> 19:37.820
You liar!

19:38.570 --> 19:40.320
Go Bąda!

19:40.730 --> 19:42.810
Are you sure you won't

19:43.070 --> 19:45.240
Connected

19:43.110 --> 19:45.240
look better without your wig?

19:45.960 --> 19:48.040
Go daddy issues!

19:48.430 --> 19:50.950
Miserable lives bring love.

19:51.250 --> 19:53.410
Share the love, and see the

19:53.410 --> 19:56.020
flowers bloom in the girls' night out!

19:57.790 --> 20:00.880
To be honest, if you haven't
even discovered me,

20:01.280 --> 20:03.390
you aren't a god yet!

20:03.630 --> 20:05.140
Go, go!

20:05.440 --> 20:08.080
Honestly, is it because I won't get more than

20:08.080 --> 20:10.390
one song that I haven't gotten a solo yet?

20:10.630 --> 20:14.040
Am I really a one-hit wonder?

20:14.040 --> 20:15.400
Keep it coming!

20:15.650 --> 20:18.350
Honestly, the smell coming
from this photo...

20:18.350 --> 20:19.530
Wealth?

20:19.530 --> 20:22.920
Is it the stench of money?

20:22.920 --> 20:24.660
Let it free!

20:25.090 --> 20:27.920
Love someone and love yourself.

20:27.920 --> 20:30.290
That's why we tell the truth.

20:30.610 --> 20:34.290
Share the love!

20:35.590 --> 20:37.040
Honestly, I want you to

20:37.040 --> 20:41.010
go out with me!

20:42.850 --> 20:44.410
Well said.

20:59.950 --> 21:00.780
What...

21:01.100 --> 21:02.340
...have...

21:02.640 --> 21:04.210
...we just...

21:04.470 --> 21:05.800
...said?

21:13.910 --> 21:17.090
What did I just say?

21:17.420 --> 21:19.540
It's all because of the Musik.

21:19.540 --> 21:21.560
I'm sure Bach-sama understands.

21:22.330 --> 21:25.880
Besides, it's because of the girls' day out.

21:29.490 --> 21:30.270
Yeah.

21:31.370 --> 21:34.340
I'm glad you both came.

21:35.420 --> 21:37.800
I feel better, somehow.

21:38.100 --> 21:41.620
I don't know if we'll be friend
or foe, next time we meet,

21:42.330 --> 21:43.810
but we'll meet again.

21:44.180 --> 21:45.230
We will.

21:45.550 --> 21:46.880
H-Hey...

21:47.920 --> 21:50.280
I'm a fan of...

21:54.040 --> 21:56.350
Thanks for supporting us.

22:02.050 --> 22:03.950
Three packs of gyoza.

22:03.950 --> 22:05.790
You're still eating?

22:05.790 --> 22:07.050
It's for everyone.

22:07.830 --> 22:11.020
We left the mansion kids out today.

22:11.320 --> 22:12.870
What could we do?

22:12.870 --> 22:13.810
It was a girls' day out.

22:15.290 --> 22:16.520
I just realized today.

22:16.820 --> 22:19.770
At a girls' day out, it doesn't matter
whether you're a boy or a girl.

22:19.770 --> 22:20.550
What?

22:20.550 --> 22:24.050
Wear whatever you're comfortable wearing,

22:24.050 --> 22:26.070
eat whatever you like, and say what you mean.

22:26.670 --> 22:29.830
If you can do that, you're
in a girls' night out.

22:39.420 --> 22:43.000
Honestly, girls' days out are awesome.

24:15.970 --> 24:26.980
09: "Beyond the Darkness"

24:16.560 --> 24:18.720
Deep, deep, in the bowels of the heart,

24:18.720 --> 24:20.680
something is astir, something is about.

24:20.870 --> 24:23.020
Is it the beginning of an ominous future?

24:23.020 --> 24:24.800
Or is it a wound of days gone by?

24:24.800 --> 24:26.810
If it must be, then it must be.

24:26.810 --> 24:29.260
Bring arrows, bring guns!
